        {
          "id": "the_activity_chain_reproduces_the_worked_examples",
          "description": "docs/process-refueling.md 6.1, at the four named stages a wrong factor shows up at. The activity half is shared: both refueling processes are weighted by the same source-hours-operating that the Total Energy Consumption they chain off is, so an error here moves all 336 rows. travelFraction normalised over the whole HPMS group is 1.609175e-03 for the oldest cohort; over source type 21 alone it is 4.10e-03 and every row is 2.55x high. averageSpeed is the ARITHMETIC mean. The four `sho` values are the snapshot's own, to its six stored significant figures.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-06
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_travelFraction",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.01804420293236,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_travelFraction",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.001609174853309,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 41
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_averageSpeed",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 56.361205525,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_sho",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 260.057,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_sho",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 83.6255,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 21
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.act_sho",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 23.1918,
              "coords": {
                "activity_rows": 41
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_energy_spine_is_running_exhaust_alone_and_reproduces_the_generator_table",
          "description": "Two claims, and they are checked together because the second is the evidence for the first.\n\n`rtDay_meanBaseRate` on the 9101 rows IS `baserate_1_2020.meanBaseRate`, the reference's own S14 intermediate, computed here from `driveschedulesecond`'s 63,602 speeds. That is the same check `mixed-onroad` and `process-brakewear` make, at the same hour, and it is what says the energy this fixture chains off is right before any refueling arithmetic touches it.\n\nAND IT IS EXACTLY ZERO ON THE OTHER TWO ENERGY POLLUTANT-PROCESSES. 9102 has 12,160 `emissionrate` rows and 104 of the run's cohorts match one of its source bins, so the rate lookup is not what stops it: its rates are on operating modes 101-108, extended idle's on mode 200, and `dc_W` is the drive-cycle distribution over the 23 RUNNING modes of an on-network road type, so the contraction has no partner. In the reference the same rows are discarded one step earlier, by `BaseRateCalculator`'s join to `runSpecRoadType` -- start rates are emitted off-network and this run selects road type 4 alone. The two mechanisms agree HERE because no off-network road type is selected; on a run that selected one they would not, and this test would fail.\n\nThe zero is asserted at three sampled rate rows of 9102 and 9190; the whole-spine energy total that made it not a sampled one is gone from the model.\n\n`rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj` is the incremental A/C load of sbweighted.rs:459. It reaches nothing -- the A/C factor is exactly 0 at this heat index -- but the generator table carries it in its own column, so it is checked here rather than left uncomputed. The tolerance is the reference's six-significant-figure column storage.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-05
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 176680.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 657,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 333651.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 697,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 118.543,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 744,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 19.1615,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 800,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 11470.2,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 738,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 26899.6,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 657,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 51142.5,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 697,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRateACAdj",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2.52938,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 800,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 821,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 861,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rtDay_meanBaseRate",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 985,
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_short_model_year_group_is_a_property_of_the_pollutant_process",
          "description": "The one cohort key that is a property of the pollutant-process rather than of the cohort, and the reason the rate stage rides a flat (pollutant-process x cohort) relation rather than widening the cohort's own columns (docs/esm-conventions.md 27.1). `pollutantprocessmodelyear` maps model year 1980 to modelYearGroup 1980 for the energy pollutant-processes, whose `shortModYrGroupID` is 80 -- a two-digit year -- and to modelYearGroup 19781995 for the refueling ones, whose short group is 52; at 1998 the two are 98 and 5300. Model year 2020 is 40 for both, which is why the pair has to be checked at more than one model year to be checked at all. A two-dimensional column keyed on both would not be a join key: `join.rs` resolves a key through a declared 1-D variable's single axis.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 40.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 657
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 80.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 697
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 98.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 679
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 40.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 52.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 41
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 5300.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 23
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_shortModYrGroupID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 52.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 205
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_EV_temperature_arm_is_live_at_this_hour_and_the_AC_arm_is_not",
          "description": "The two clamps of S15, at 59.5 degF, on the energy spine this fixture chains off. The A/C activity quadratic is -0.29698 and clamps to 0, so the A/C factor is exactly 0.\n\nTHE EV TEMPERATURE ARM DOES NOT CLAMP. (59.5 - 72)(0.00225 + 0.00028 x (59.5 - 72)) = +0.015625, positive, so the factor is 1.015625 on every electricity energy row. Two things had to be right to get there: the temperatureadjustment row is keyed regClassID 0, a WILDCARD, and reaching it needs the two-step precedence of lib/adjustments.esm's `exact_else_wildcard` -- with the exact-class lookup alone the terms come out 0, the raw adjustment 0, and the answer is 1 for the wrong reason and 1.56 % low; and the branch is gated on pollutant 91 AND process 1 together (adjust.rs:107), so the SAME electricity cohort on a refueling rate row takes the standard quadratic instead and its factor is exactly 1.\n\nWHAT THIS TEST CANNOT DO IS SEE ITSELF IN THE OUTPUT, and that is stated here rather than left to be discovered (docs/esm-conventions.md 23). A refueling row sums the energy of its OWN (modelYearID, fuelTypeID) cohort, and every electricity cohort is dropped by REFEC-7's fuel-type join, so no fuel-9 energy reaches an emitted cell: perturbing the temperature terms or `evefficiency` moves none of this fixture's 336 rows. Both are asserted at the rate-relation column, where they are computed and worth pinning; the checks that bite are components/onroad_energy_output.esm's and fixtures/process-brakewear.esm's, where the same arm moves 84 output cells.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 2e-06
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_acActivityRaw",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": -0.2969815,
              "coords": {
                "runspeccounty_rows": 1,
                "runspecmonth_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_acActivity",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspeccounty_rows": 1,
                "runspecmonth_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.run_evTemperatureIsSuppressed",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspeccounty_rows": 1,
                "runspecsourcetype_rows": 1,
                "runspecmonth_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_hasTempAdjustExact",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 800
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_tempAdjustTermA",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.00225,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 800
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_tempAdjustTermB",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.00028,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 800
              }
            },
            {
